{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 4, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 5145515057632340370, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 631, "mtime": 1791871701.697931, "sha256": "7913f05f503d3c1f82df1efc68f1cca2fc98454d732b2475211bdac9675f916e"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 404, "mtime": 1791871711.614545, "sha256": "363331fb90fc09eca5f0c8c6698b70843d8730019bd43a1b9f036088d9d139b9"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/3/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/3/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Why it was wrong:** the old code was `round(x, 2)`, and two things broke it:\n- As a binary float, `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so it falls just below the halfway point.\n- Python's `round()` rounds exact halves to the even digit, so `0.125 \u2192 0.12`. The docstring promises half-up rounding.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now converts `repr(x)` to a `Decimal` and rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. `repr(x)` gives the shortest decimal string that converts back to the same float, so `2.675` becomes `\"2.675\"` and rounds up as expected. It still returns a `float`, so callers like `add_vat` see the same return type as before.\n\n**Checks:**\n- Ran by hand: `2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `0.135\u21920.14`, `-2.675\u2192-2.68`, `2.674\u21922.67`, `add_vat(10)\u219212.0`.\n- Added a regression test in `tests/test_round_money.py`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I called the new test and the existing `tests/test_split.py::test_split` directly with `python3`. Both passed.\n\n**Behaviour change:** negative halves now round away from zero (`-2.675 \u2192 -2.68`), which matches what \"half up\" usually means for money.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 10, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 277972, "requests_cache_write": 9412, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1469224, "requests_count": 10, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_output": 2209, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial3", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 4, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T06:08:07.340301+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls":